+/*
+	Resonance: games on network shares (see netfs.h).
+
+	One connection per share, opened when first needed and kept (a mutex per share: libnfs' and
+	libsmb2's synchronous calls aren't thread-safe on one context). A broken connection is closed
+	and opened again on the next call; a share that can't be reached isn't tried again for 20 s
+	(the library scanner asks often).
+
+	Files are read in 1 MiB pieces kept in a small cache, and the piece after the one just read is
+	fetched in the background, so a game reading its disc in order mostly finds the data there.
+
