+/*
+	Resonance updates from the project's GitHub releases, the way DolphinPS4 does it
+	(DolphinNoGUI/PS4Updater.cpp): the latest release is compared with the running version and its
+	files are downloaded, the connection's certificate checked and each file checked against the
+	SHA-256 GitHub publishes for it.
+
+	A release has the full package (Resonance-vXX.YY.pkg) and an update archive
+	(Resonance-vXX.YY-update.tar: eboot.bin, version.txt, launcher/). The archive is unpacked into
+	/data/Resonance/app, and from the next start the installed app starts the newer program from
+	there (startDownloadedUpdate); its pictures, fonts and sounds come from there too
+	(ps4_app_dir). The running app can't install a package over itself: a release without an
+	archive leaves its checked package in /data/pkg for the Package Installer.
+
+	This file is part of Flycast.
+
